# P5: extension-entity same-module simplification
# Date: 2026-04-26
# Baseline (P4): 21.21% (13526/63757)
# Result (P5):   32.55% (20754/63757)
# Gain:          +7228 symbols (+11.34%)

## Changes

### stable.go
- tryExtensionEntity: 4 same-module simplification paths
  - Change 1 (accessor vg/vs/vM/vw/vW): sig=="" → hostName+extMarker+"."+declName+accessor
  - Change 2 (vpMV descriptor + vp stored): sig=="" → simplified, no type annotation
  - Change 3 (init fC/fc): sig=="" → hostName+extMarker+".init"+labelStr
  - Change 4 (F entity): sig=="" → new same-module block with label-only format
  - extMarker logic: Rz→"<A>", len(constraintBytes)>2→"<>", else ""
  - sig!="" (inverse/same-type constraints) → verbose preserved (corpus symbols)

- tryVariableEntity: module stripping for vg/vs/vM/vw/vW (background agent addition)
  - Non-Foundation modules: strip module prefix, no type annotation
  - Static+module+type format preserved for all others

- tryEntitySuffix: M*/W* suffix module stripping (background agent addition)
  - descriptorPrintOpts(): Foundation/Swift→full-qualified, concurrency/others→simplified
  - swift.prerendered attr prevents double-printing by printer.go

- tryFunctionEntity: REVERTED background agent's simplified rendering block
  - Plain functions still use verbose format (module + full types + return type)
  - Required: Apple corpus expects "example.f() async -> ()" not "f()"

### common/{node,substitution,printer}.go (background agent additions, kept)
- node.go: ModuleOf() utility for descriptor formatters
- substitution.go: IsConcurrencyType() + concurrency tag on Sc<X> types
- printer.go: swift.prerendered attr support

### stable_test.go
- Updated M/W descriptor tests: "main.Foo" → "Foo" (module stripped)
- Updated mCases: Sc types now "Actor"/"Task" not "Swift.Actor"/"Swift.Task"
- Updated varGeneric accessor tests: "Foo.n.getter" not "main.Foo.n.getter : Swift.Int"

### testdata/swiftc/swiftc-oracle-divergences.txt
- Added 2 Protocols symbols (swiftc oracle still verbose)

